text.section:
An out-of-state supplier who elects to be licensed as a permissive supplier shall comply with (i) the same requirements imposed on a supplier and (ii) all of the following with respect to motor fuel that is removed by the permissive supplier at a terminal located in another state and has Virginia as its destination state:

Collect the tax due the Commonwealth on the fuel;


Waive any defense that the Commonwealth lacks jurisdiction to require the supplier to collect the tax due the Commonwealth on the motor fuel under this chapter;


Report and pay the tax due on the fuel in the same manner as if the removal had occurred at a terminal located in Virginia;


Keep records of the removal of the fuel and submit to audits concerning the fuel as if the removal had occurred at a terminal located in Virginia; and


Report sales by the supplier to a person who is not licensed in the state where the removal occurred if the destination state is Virginia.
